# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.pipeline (M4-S3).
#
# This file is load-bearing, not hygiene. The repo is 5.2 GB on disk and 3.5 GB
# of that is data/ (2.0 GB of DVC-pinned parquet) plus .venv/ (1.5 GB of wheels
# the image resolves for itself). A build without these exclusions ships both to
# the daemon before the first instruction runs.
#
# Rule of thumb for anything added later: the image may contain CODE, CONFIG and
# the LOCKFILE. Data reaches tasks at run time (M4-S4's decision: MinIO or a
# mounted path), never by being baked in — data is DVC's to pin, and an image
# carrying a copy of it would be a second, unpinned definition of the dataset.

# THE RULE, and it was learned the hard way. This file's first draft excluded
# `data/` wholesale, and the in-image unit suite went red on 24 tests: 1.1 MB of
# `data/reference/` is COMMITTED — the zone centroids, the TLC zone lookup, the
# pinned `taxi_zones.zip`, the federal-holiday table — and it is not "data" in the
# DVC sense at all, it is the lookup layer `taxi_mlops.features` reads at fit time
# and (from M5) at serving time. Excluding it produced an image that imports fine
# and cannot build a feature.
#
# So the rule is: **the image contains what git contains.** The exclusions below
# are the repo's own ignore rules (root .gitignore + data/.gitignore) plus the
# build-context-only entries (.git, .github). Anything a `git clone` would give
# you is in the image; anything DVC pins, a build produces, or a session logs is
# not. That also makes this file checkable — tests/unit/test_task_image.py asserts
# every path data/.gitignore names is excluded here and that data/reference is not.

# --- the big ones: DVC's, exactly as data/.gitignore names them ---
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/rejected/
# The scoring trees (M7-S1) — DVC's, exactly as data/.gitignore names them.
# 15.4M rows of 2020 that a task pod reads off the staged PVC like every other
# tree, never out of the image.
data/scoring/
data/scoring_rejected/
# `make contract-probe`'s throwaway acquisition dir (M7-S1): a real TLC file
# downloaded to be measured. Not DVC's, not the repo's, and not the image's.
data/probe/
data/predictions/
# Model output on the scoring months (M7-S2), on data/predictions/'s terms.
data/scoring_predictions/
data/analyst.duckdb
data/analyst.duckdb.wal
.venv/

# --- host-resolved state the image must rebuild, not inherit ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dvc/cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/
mlruns/

# --- secrets: never, under any circumstances, in an image layer ---
# `.env.example` is the exception and it is deliberate: it holds no secret (it is
# the committed TEMPLATE), and tests/unit/test_marts.py asserts it documents the
# marts credentials — a test that went red in-image when a `.env.*` glob ate it.
.env
!.env.example

# --- history, run logs and editor state: no bearing on what the image runs ---
.git/
.github/
automation/logs/
automation/runs/
analytics/dbt/target/
analytics/dbt/logs/
analytics/dbt/dbt_packages/
analytics/dbt/marts.duckdb
analytics/dbt/marts.duckdb.wal
.idea/
.verify_m1_sandbox/
notebooks/
